@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Desktop search, preserved views and cached selection
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Contributor
participant "app : App" as App
participant "dataset\n<<module>>" as Dataset
activate Contributor
Contributor -> App : _refresh_browse_list()
activate App
App -> Dataset : load_all() through _load_entries()
activate Dataset
note over Dataset : Same-path lock; validate header and row shape.\nLegacy metadata is normalized only in memory.
Dataset --> App : Entries or storage exception
deactivate Dataset
alt Read failed
  note over App : Report Dataset unavailable; do not clear the tree,\ncache, selection or unsaved editor fields.
else Read succeeded
  note over App : Strip/casefold query; replace tree and cache.\nCache every loaded row by ID, not only visible matches.
  loop Each entry
    alt Query empty or substring in any stored value
      note over App : Insert a visible tree row.
    else No match
      note over App : Keep cached, omit from visible tree.
    end
  end
  note over App : If the selected ID disappeared, report it;\nretain unsaved edits for recovery.
end
App --> Contributor : Matching rows or retained view + error
deactivate App
opt Contributor selects a visible row
  Contributor -> App : _on_browse_select(event)
  activate App
  App -> App : _populate_browse_entry(cached entry)
  activate App
  note over App : Fill evidence/review controls, ID and audio reference.\nUnchanged legacy strings are preserved.
  App --> App : Selection and controls synchronized
  deactivate App
  App --> Contributor : Editable selection, with no second CSV read
  deactivate App
end
deactivate Contributor
legend bottom
  IDs should remain unique; manually corrupted identifiers are not repaired here.
  Filtering is read-only. Empty results are distinct from a failed read.
endlegend
@enduml
